# Agent Instructions
Describe this project's purpose, implementation boundaries, and local rules here. Adapt this template; do not leave placeholders as active instructions.

## Workflow source
This project adopts `project-workflows/`. Read its `workflow.toml` for configured document locations, then use its `<skill-name>/SKILL.md` procedures. The project-specific copy is authoritative over global seeds. Project instructions override seed defaults. General skills and external-service tooling are optional unless explicitly adopted.

For an ordinary adopting project, the workflow adaptation branch lives inside that submodule; it is separate from this repository's branch. Record the actual platform-neutral branch name during adoption. Use the adopted update procedure for shared improvements, project reconciliation, branch-name metadata, and exact consumer pins. Publication scope and remote availability must be verified separately. If this checkout is explicitly designated as the canonical maintenance/global installation, record shared `main` instead and retain neutral configuration; this exception does not remove project branches from other adoptions.

## Documentation
README explains the project and how to start. TODO indexes active work. Current policies define standing guidance; spike pairs hold scoped reasoning and work state; scratch is provisional; archives preserve history. Actual project documents live in this repository, outside the workflow submodule. Use `capture-for-later` for individual scratch notes when saving a possibility or deliberately parking a subject. A new note uses only `status: captured` or `status: parked` unless local conventions differ; one sentence is enough. Keep known reasoning and optional revisit conditions without inventing them. Capture does not create tasks or a spike; `run-project-spike` runs active bounded workstreams. Preserve existing notes and legacy lists rather than migrating them during setup.

## Validation and Git
Record the actual validation commands and commit/review policy. Preserve concurrent work. Review scoped diffs before committing; never include private configuration or credentials. Publishing and remote actions follow the user's authorization and repository policy.

## Markdown style
Keep each prose paragraph or comment paragraph on one line and let editors wrap it. Avoid reflow-only edits. Preserve meaningful line breaks, existing local conventions, and explicit formatter requirements.
